9:- `Conversation` (`packages/frontend/conversation.ts`) — owns a `MessageParam[]`, the streaming accumulator, `messages`, `inFlight`, `send(text)`, `onChange`. `MODEL`, `MAX_TOKENS` and `SYSTEM` are module constants; `SYSTEM` is deliberately task mode.
11:- `AppView` (`packages/frontend/view.ts`) — the whole prototype-1 shell: mode toggle, transcript `bindList`, composer, `readAnchor`/`resolvePoint` selection capture, and a `bindSlot` holding `LearningPane`.
31:`Conversation` grows a `hiddenTurns` count so those seed turns are excluded from `messages`; the pane therefore shows the assistant's answer first, and anchor offsets keep indexing the list the user can actually see, at every depth. This is the only change to `conversation.ts` beyond making `system` a constructor option.
41:Two visual states matter: the *live* selection the user just dragged (no thread yet) and *committed* marks (a thread exists). The active thread's mark is emphasized further, so the user can see which highlight the right pane belongs to.
45:The app shows two panes. `focus` is the thread on the left; the thread on the right is `focus.activeChild`. Both panes are the same `ThreadView`: transcript, marks, selection capture, composer, and — when that pane holds a live selection — the action menu.
47:- Selecting in the **left** pane and picking an action creates a child of `focus` and makes it active: the right pane fills in.
48:- Selecting in the **right** pane and picking an action creates a child of *that* thread, and then **shifts left**: `focus` becomes the right-hand thread, and the new child becomes the right pane. This is the "go deeper" loop, and it falls out of the model rather than needing its own machinery.
49:- Clicking any mark in the left pane activates that thread (right pane). Clicking a mark in the right pane shifts left and activates it.
51:A breadcrumb above the panes shows the path from the root to `focus`; clicking an ancestor moves `focus` back up, leaving the descendant as its active child so the right pane still shows where you were.
53:Task mode is unchanged: one pane, composer, no selection capture. Learning mode is what turns on the second pane and the marks.
136:- `activeChild` is always a member of `children`, and `focus` is always a live thread id.
137:- The right pane exists iff `focus.activeChild !== null`; the action menu renders in whichever pane owns the live selection, and at most one pane has one (starting a selection in a pane clears the other's).
156:  - Playwright: with two committed marks in one message, both are visible and clicking each dispatches the right thread — verified through the observable effect (the right pane's content changes).
